      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/library"
      ],
      "description": "Ingested L1 source material for the sciences. `milnorlink` was the whole of it until 2026-09-29, when three Lean-autoformalization papers arrived as the `evidence` of this layer's methodology nodes (bean h3rw). `milnorlink` is the source text the derived `milnor` skill reads, moved out of cat-harness/library/ because the PLATFORM holds no content (bean r1lz, and the rule AGENTS.md states as 'folio-assistant is the platform, not the content'). Its `image-verdicts.json` moved with it rather than staying behind: a verdict belongs to the library it judges, and one file judging documents in two libraries is how one library's judgement comes to rewrite another's sidecar. The id is `library`, the CONVENTIONAL one, so this entry OVERRIDES the default rather than joining it: overrides match on id and never on path, so a distinct id at the same path yields two entries for one directory and every fan-out consumer scans it twice. Measured while doing exactly that.",
      "readmePath": "library/README.md",
      "fileCount": 0,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-call-activity-click/folio-assistant-sci/directory/library",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-sci/directory/library"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-call-activity-click/folio-assistant-sci/directory/sci-extracted-references",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Subgraph",
      "name": "sci-extracted-references",
      "path": "extracted-references/",
      "contentSource": {
        "kind": "directory",
        "declaredIn": "default"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/references"
      ],
      "description": "The reference lists of the papers in `library/`, split into one folio-reference/v1 node per entry with `provenance: extracted` (bean folio-assistant-63q4). Each node is `<doc-id>.r<n>.json`, `<n>` being the printed number of a numbered list (so `[12]` in a paper's text is `.r12`) or the position in an author-year one; `derivedFrom` names the section file the entry was read from. GENERATED by scripts/extract-references.ts from the library text, never hand-edited: `check:extracted-references` fails on any difference. The text is PDF extraction, so the raw entry is always kept whole in `note`, and `title`, `author`, `issued`, `DOI` and `URL` are set only where the entry's shape makes them unambiguous; a field the extractor could not read with confidence is absent, not guessed. Declared WITH its files, per bean dh4f. Listed and exported, with every other `references` directory, by folio-assistant-core's bibliography viewer.",
      "readmePath": "extracted-references/README.md",
      "fileCount": 0,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-call-activity-click/folio-assistant-sci/directory/sci-extracted-references",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-sci/directory/sci-extracted-references"
