        "declaredIn": "default"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns#graphTypology/code"
      ],
      "description": "The PAPER content adapter — `PaperContentAdapter` and its Lean tool registrar. It arrived here 2026-09-30 (bean y5si, step 1 of 2 on the owner's Option A ruling on issue #1558), and the destination was not a judgement made at the time: `cat-harness/src/builtin-adapters.ts` already declared this adapter `layer: \"sci\"`, and `cat-harness/scripts/partition/instance-rules.ts` already listed the prefix `adapters/paper/` in its `repo: \"sci\"` block. Two existing machine-readable classifications that the DIRECTORY had simply never matched; the directory caught up with them. This is the first EXECUTABLE TypeScript this instance holds beyond `contributions.ts`, which is why `tsconfig.json`'s `include` gained `folio-assistant-sci/adapters/**/*.ts` in the same commit as the move — bean `lvoa` measured what happens when it does not: a file crossing an instance boundary leaves the typecheck program and no gate reports a shrinking one. `dependents: skip` because a dependent gets its adapter by DECLARING a `contentType`, resolved through `BUILTIN_ADAPTERS` by variable path, rather than by inheriting this directory to scan. `adapters/document/` is NOT here and is not coming in this change: it is step 2, and moving it alongside is what takes the instance-boundary import axis through 16 instead of leaving it at 2.",
      "readmePath": "adapters/README.md",
      "fileCount": 0,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-call-activity-click/folio-assistant-sci/directory/sci-adapters",
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-sci/directory/sci-adapters"
    },
